{"version": "6.9", "hitCount": 3, "request": {"queryString": "\"TP63\" AND lacrimal AND \"Homo sapiens\"[Organism]", "resultType": "core", "cursorMark": "*", "pageSize": 5, "sort": "", "synonym": false}, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "41876478", "source": "MED", "pmid": "41876478", "pmcid": "PMC13039162", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC13039162"]}, "doi": "10.1038/s41420-026-03060-8", "title": "p63 in skin homeostasis and disease: molecular mechanisms and therapeutic potentials.", "authorString": "Cong Y, He Z, Hao H, Chen H, Chen A, Li C, Hu Y, Cong X.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Cong Y", "lastName": "Cong", "firstName": "Yujia", "initials": "Y", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Dermatology, China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Changchun, China."}]}}, {"fullName": "He Z", "lastName": "He", "firstName": "Zhenglin", "initials": "Z", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0004-9708-0605"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China. CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}}, {"fullName": "Hao H", "lastName": "Hao", "firstName": "Hanming", "initials": "H", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "College of Basic Medical Sciences, Jilin University, Changchun, China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Chen H", "lastName": "Chen", "firstName": "Haoran", "initials": "H", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Chen A", "lastName": "Chen", "firstName": "Anqi", "initials": "A", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Dermatology, China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Changchun, China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Li C", "lastName": "Li", "firstName": "Chunyi", "initials": "C", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7275-4440"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Institute of Antler Science and Product Technology, Changchun Sci-Tech University, Changchun, China."}]}}, {"fullName": "Hu Y", "lastName": "Hu", "firstName": "Yue", "initials": "Y", "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China. CONTACT_EMAIL."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Biobank, China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Changchun, China. CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}}, {"fullName": "Cong X", "lastName": "Cong", "firstName": "Xianling", "initials": "X", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5790-4188"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China. CONTACT_EMAIL."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Dermatology, China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Changchun, China. CONTACT_EMAIL."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Biobank, China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Changchun, China. CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7275-4440"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-5790-4188"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0009-0004-9708-0605"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "12", "journalIssueId": 4148544, "dateOfPublication": "2026 Mar", "monthOfPublication": 3, "yearOfPublication": 2026, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Cell Death Discov", "title": "Cell death discovery", "essn": "2058-7716", "issn": "2058-7716", "nlmid": "101665035", "isoabbreviation": "Cell Death Discov"}, "printPublicationDate": "2026-03-01"}, "pubYear": "2026", "pageInfo": "154", "abstractText": "As a pivotal member of the p53 family, the p63 gene plays an indispensable role in skin homeostasis and development. The gene encodes multiple isoforms, primarily TAp63 and \u0394Np63, which differentially regulate cell proliferation, differentiation, and stress responses through complementary mechanisms. This comprehensive review systematically examines the molecular mechanisms and cellular functions of p63 in cutaneous biology, with particular emphasis on its dual roles in maintaining skin integrity and contributing to disease pathogenesis. We detail the essential functions of p63 in skin development, encompassing epithelial fate determination, chromatin remodeling, cell adhesion, and barrier formation, while also exploring its involvement in skin regeneration and differentiation via metabolic reprogramming and stem cell modulation. Furthermore, we analyze how mutations in p63 underlie ectodermal dysplasia and various dermatological disorders, underscoring the gene's fundamental importance in cutaneous health. By integrating current knowledge of the diverse biological roles of p63 and its associated therapeutic potential as a target, this review highlights its central significance in both skin physiology and pathology.", "affiliation": "China-Japan Union Hospital of Jilin University, Jilin University, Changchun, China.", "publicationStatus": "epublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41420-026-03060-8"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13039162"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentSt